course: dictionary
lesson: 14775
title: Provision: supplies, plans and rules
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Provision is a useful word with a few meanings. Most often it means supplies, or the act of giving something people need. «The explorers packed provisions for the long journey across the ice.» Provisions here are the food and drink they carried, because a journey needs supplies.
explain: Provision can also mean a plan made before something happens. «The town made provision for bad weather by storing food and building a shelter.» The town planned ahead in case the bad weather came. The phrase make provision for always means planning for something that might happen.
explain: In formal writing, a provision can be a rule or condition in a law or agreement. «One provision of the new law says every school must have a nurse.» Here the word means a rule. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: food and drink, planning ahead, or a rule in a law.
fact: Provision means giving or supplying something people need.
fact: Provisions (plural) means supplies of food and drink for a journey.
fact: «Make provision for» means plan ahead for something that might happen.
fact: In a law or agreement, a provision is a rule or condition.
fact: Provision is a noun and can also be a verb, but the verb is formal and used mostly in official writing.
exercise: «The sailors packed provisions for the long voyage.» What are provisions here? | Songs for the crew | * Supplies of food and drink | Ropes and sails | A map of the sea
exercise: «The council made provision for bad weather by building a shelter.» What does made provision mean? | Painted the shelter | Forgot about the weather | Asked the weather to stop | * Made a plan for something that might happen
exercise: A camp has provisions for 10 people for 5 days. What does provisions mean in this maths problem? | * Food and drink supplied for the group | Tents for sleeping | Pets kept on the farm | Money for the trip
test: «The shop's provision of fresh water helped the whole village.» What does provision mean here? | * Giving or supplying something people need | Painting the shop | A small lake | Stopping the water
test: Ben runs out of provisions halfway up the mountain. What has he run out of? | Maps of the area | Warm socks | * Supplies of food and drink | Friends to walk with
exam: «Under one provision of the agreement, both countries must share their water.» What is a provision in this sentence? | A type of small boat | * A rule or condition | A picnic on the beach | A kind of wet weather
